     If the --MM option is specified, the aarr utility will read and execute com‐
     mands from its standard input.  If standard input is a terminal, the aarr
     utility will display the prompt “AR >” before reading a line, and will
     continue operation even if errors are encountered.  If standard input is
     not a terminal, the aarr utility will not display a prompt and will termi‐
     nate execution on encountering an error.

     Each input line contains a single command.  Words in an input line are
     separated by whitespace characters.  The first word of the line is the
     command, the remaining words are the arguments to the command.  The com‐
     mand word may be specified in either case.  Arguments may be separated by
     commas or blanks.

     Empty lines are allowed and are ignored.  Long lines are continued by
     ending them with the “+” character.

     The “*” and “;” characters start a comment.  Comments extend till the end
     of the line.

     When executing an MRI librarian script the aarr utility works on a tempo‐
     rary copy of an archive.  Changes to the copy are made permanent using
     the ssaavvee command.

     Commands understood by the aarr utility are:

     aaddddlliibb _a_r_c_h_i_v_e | aaddddlliibb _a_r_c_h_i_v_e (_m_e_m_b_e_r [, _m_e_m_b_e_r]...)
             Add the contents of the archive named by argument _a_r_c_h_i_v_e to the
             current archive.  If specific members are named using the argu‐
             ments _m_e_m_b_e_r, then those members are added to the current ar‐
             chive.  If no members are specified, the entire contents of the
             archive are added to the current archive.

     aaddddmmoodd _m_e_m_b_e_r [, _m_e_m_b_e_r]...
             Add the files named by arguments _m_e_m_b_e_r to the current archive.

     cclleeaarr   Discard all the contents of the current archive.

     ccrreeaattee _a_r_c_h_i_v_e
             Create a new archive named by the argument _a_r_c_h_i_v_e, and makes it
             the current archive.  If the named archive already exists, it
             will be overwritten when the ssaavvee command is issued.

     ddeelleettee _m_o_d_u_l_e [, _m_e_m_b_e_r]...
             Delete the modules named by the arguments _m_e_m_b_e_r from the current
             archive.

     ddiirreeccttoorryy _a_r_c_h_i_v_e (_m_e_m_b_e_r [, _m_e_m_b_e_r]...) [_o_u_t_p_u_t_f_i_l_e]
             List each named module in the archive.  The format of the output
             depends on the verbosity setting set using the vveerrbboossee command.
             Output is sent to standard output, or to the file specified by
             argument _o_u_t_p_u_t_f_i_l_e.

     eenndd     Exit successfully from the aarr utility.  Any unsaved changes to
             the current archive will be discarded.

     eexxttrraacctt _m_e_m_b_e_r [, _m_e_m_b_e_r]...
             Extract the members named by the arguments _m_e_m_b_e_r from the cur‐
             rent archive.

     lliisstt    Display the contents of the current archive in verbose style.

     ooppeenn _a_r_c_h_i_v_e
             Open the archive named by argument _a_r_c_h_i_v_e and make it the cur‐
             rent archive.

     rreeppllaaccee _m_e_m_b_e_r [, _m_e_m_b_e_r]...
             Replace named members in the current archive with the files spec‐
             ified by arguments _m_e_m_b_e_r.  The files must be present in the cur‐
             rent directory and the named modules must already exist in the
             current archive.

     ssaavvee    Commit all changes to the current archive.

     vveerrbboossee
             Toggle the verbosity of the ddiirreeccttoorryy command.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     To create a new archive _e_x_._a containing three files _e_x_1_._o, _e_x_2_._o and
     _e_x_3_._o, use:
           ar -rc ex.a ex1.o ex2.o ex3.o

     To add an archive symbol table to an existing archive _e_x_._a, use:
           ar -s ex.a

     To delete file _e_x_1_._o from archive _e_x_._a, use:
           ar -d ex.a ex1.o

     To verbosely list the contents of archive _e_x_._a, use:
           ar -tv ex.a

     To create a new archive _e_x_._a containing the files _e_x_1_._o, and _e_x_2_._o, using
     MRI librarian commands, use the following script:

           create ex.a              * specify the output archive
           addmod ex1.o ex2.o       * add modules
           save                     * save pending changes
           end                      * exit the utility

